Luanati server
---

Manually create config before starting container.

See docker instructions for reference: https://docs.luanti.org/for-server-hosts/setup/containers/

cd services/config
mkdir luanati
cd luanati
mkdir -p config data/.minetest/{games,mods}

Copy example config to config/minetest.conf and edit as appropriate.
> https://github.com/luanti-org/luanti/blob/master/minetest.conf.example

cd data/.mintest/games
git clone https://github.com/luanti-org/minetest_game
git clone https://codeberg.org/mineclonia/mineclonia
git clone https://github.com/asuna-mt/asuna

# Nasty, but have to do it because it's not possible to set different permissions on the directory tree as they suggest when using podman - causes an OCI error. Do not do this if running a public server.
chmod -R 777 data/
